<title>SINGAPORE: SPH '96 net profit down 1.1 pct.</title>
<headline>SPH '96 net profit down 1.1 pct.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1996-11-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to August 31 1996</p>
<p>		   (in millions of S$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit		     307.63	vs   310.98</p>
<p>    Group shr (cents)	     90.1	 vs    91.2</p>
<p>    Dividend (final, cents)     20.0	 vs    20.0</p>
<p>    Turnover			 891.04	vs    833.34</p>
<p>    Pretax profit		  423.56	vs    425.95</p>
<p>    Associates			 6.96(loss)vs	4.40 (loss)</p>
<p>    Investment income	     52.95	vs     53.16</p>
<p>    Minorities			 0.32	vs	0.86 (loss)</p>
<p>    Extraordinaries		  0.70(loss)vs	0.95 (gain)</p>
<p>Div Register  - January 20 1997</p>
<p>Dividend pay  - January 29 1997</p>
<p>Note - Singapore Press Holdings said extraordinary items were due to writeoff of goodwill on acquisitions of certain subsidiaries. Share of loss from associates was due mainly to investment in newly started multimedia companies.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom (65 8703080)</p>
</text>
